WEBVTT


00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:35.065
You were right.
Earth won't make it.


00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:38.405
Even the last ones who
escaped earth arrived.


00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.711
But there is no more
place in here either.


00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:46.163
The epidemics are
spreading faster.


00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.712
I'm not able to keep up.


00:04:49.747 --> 00:04:52.961
The people are dying in my arms.


00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.565
I applied as a doctor
on a cargo ship.


00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:08.335
Four years until we are
there and 4 years back.


00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:12.070
I'll spend most of the
time in hibernation.


00:05:12.105 --> 00:05:13.665
This single flight...


00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.200
...and I'll have
enough money to...


00:05:15.235 --> 00:05:17.465
...go to Rhea.


00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.533
Then we'll finally
be together again.


00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:29.172
Did you hear my dear
sister? I have to go.


00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.265
I want to get to Rhea.


00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.577
And finally see you
and the kids again.


00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.665
Dr. Laura Portmann?


00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:46.300
Anna Lindbergh, first officer.


00:07:46.335 --> 00:07:48.580
Welcome aboard.


00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.700
Everybody listen.


00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:26.200
Miyuki Yoshida,
system administrator.


00:08:26.235 --> 00:08:28.965
This loudmouth here is Vespucci.


00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.631
Thankfully Prokoff
isn't talking that much.


00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:37.438
Dr. Portmann.


00:08:41.382 --> 00:08:44.400
Station 42 will be
upgraded to a transport hub.


00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.497
It's in the Orth's Cloud,
half way to Proxima...


00:08:52.532 --> 00:08:57.489
...and is in a stable
orbit around RH278.


00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.307
The autopilot is activated.


00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.504
Because of all the
recent terror attacks...


00:09:05.539 --> 00:09:09.000
...the temporary government
ordered to have...


00:09:09.035 --> 00:09:13.296
...a sky marshal on every ship.


00:09:13.331 --> 00:09:14.821
Damn snitches.


00:09:14.856 --> 00:09:16.938
It is said, that the
"Maschinen Stuermer" are...


00:09:16.973 --> 00:09:20.006
...preparing for
major sabotage acts.


00:09:20.041 --> 00:09:24.700
This ship is already decaying,
no one would sabotage anything.


00:09:33.373 --> 00:09:37.565
Lt. Samuel Decker.
Space Security Agency.


00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:41.750
We will seal the cargo
compartment in 30 minutes.


00:09:41.785 --> 00:09:45.900
If you want to get to know
someone, better do it now.


00:09:45.935 --> 00:09:47.365
At 0200 the engines
will started.


00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:51.490
At 0230 we will meet
at the cryo chambers.


00:09:51.525 --> 00:09:54.420
Have a good company.


00:09:57.325 --> 00:09:59.965
According to resolution
278 of the RBS...


00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.000
...from now on there will be sky
marshals even on cargo flights.


00:10:04.035 --> 00:10:07.337
Just accept me as
a part of the crew.


00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:17.165
"This is an informational
broadcast of the TSA."


00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:21.700
"The threat of terror attacks has never
been as present since the great collapse. "


00:10:21.735 --> 00:10:26.430
"Klaus Bruckner is still on the run
after his latest terror attack. "


00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:31.700
"This man is responsible
for the latest bombings...


00:10:31.735 --> 00:10:36.165
"... on the stations
20, 23 and 24."


00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.665
"While he is claiming responsibility
for the current attacks,... "


00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.421
"... he keeps on propagating the
messages of the "Maschinen Stuermer"."


00:10:43.456 --> 00:10:45.547
"We are living in machines. "


00:10:45.582 --> 00:10:48.583
"What are we
producing? Machines. "


00:10:48.618 --> 00:10:51.465
"Our enemy is the TSA."


00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:55.593
"There will be no peace as long
as technology is ruling us. "


00:10:55.628 --> 00:10:57.687
"Down with the machines!"


00:10:57.722 --> 00:10:59.712
"Down with the stations!"


00:10:59.747 --> 00:11:03.511
"Because of the latest
events, the TSA ordered,... "


00:11:03.546 --> 00:11:07.241
"... to ensure the safety
of ship and crew,... "


00:11:07.276 --> 00:11:10.700
"... each flight to be accompanied
by a security officer. "


00:11:10.735 --> 00:11:14.538
"Support the sky marshal
on his duty and... "


00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:15.867
Listen everybody, this
will be the order of shifts.


00:12:15.902 --> 00:12:19.200
Each shift will take
8 and a half months.


00:12:19.235 --> 00:12:20.867
I'll take the first.


00:12:20.902 --> 00:12:22.201
Then Lindbergh...


00:12:22.236 --> 00:12:23.418
...Yoshida...


00:12:23.453 --> 00:12:24.326
...Vespucci...


00:12:24.361 --> 00:12:25.930
...Prokoff...


00:12:25.965 --> 00:12:27.465
...Portmann.


00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:30.300
At the end to deploy the
cargo, Lindbergh again.


00:12:30.335 --> 00:12:32.413
And if someone should
face any problems,...


00:12:32.448 --> 00:12:34.491
...feel free to
knock on Deckers tank.


00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:46.700
"Dear Laura,"


00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:51.271
"I'm sending you some
sunshine from Rhea. "


00:14:53.198 --> 00:14:58.200
"I haven't had you in my
arms for such a long time... "


00:14:58.235 --> 00:15:01.200
"It's not good that you
are doing cargo flights. "


00:15:01.235 --> 00:15:03.465
"We are worried. "


00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:06.200
"People are telling each other
that the "Maschinen Stuermer"... "


00:15:06.235 --> 00:15:07.665
"... are becoming more
and more aggressive. "


00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:11.511
"But what do you expect us to believe
from four year's old information?"


00:15:11.546 --> 00:15:15.900
"I don't even want to think about what
could have happened in the mean time. "


00:15:15.935 --> 00:15:18.526
"I really hope that
you are doing well. "


00:15:18.561 --> 00:15:21.247
"Please stay in touch. "


00:15:21.282 --> 00:15:24.394
"See you soon. "


00:15:24.429 --> 00:15:27.506
"I miss you. "


00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:47.547
Dear Arianne,


00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:53.292
I miss you too.


00:16:53.327 --> 00:16:58.183
It is so unbelievable cold
in here, you couldn't imagine.


00:16:58.218 --> 00:17:02.945
I'll show you some pics of
the mess I got myself into.


00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:07.672
Well... Just two months left
till the end of my shift.


00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:12.665
We are four light
years away from earth.


00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:16.200
And are transporting
material to build a station,


00:17:16.235 --> 00:17:19.665
so that one day, we will
be able to fly to Proxima.


00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:22.700
It has been said that there
are inhabitable planets too.


00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:27.972
I really want to be with you.


00:17:28.007 --> 00:17:29.853
Please don't worry,


00:17:29.888 --> 00:17:32.254
I'm doing fine.


00:17:32.289 --> 00:17:34.620
See you soon.


00:21:26.041 --> 00:21:27.665
What are you doing here?


00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:29.700
Someone opened the
cargo compartment.


00:21:29.735 --> 00:21:32.606
I was automatically woken up.


00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:35.665
Why did you open up the gate?


00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:39.699
You know that it is strictly forbidden
to enter the cargo compartment.


00:21:39.734 --> 00:21:43.500
Something is inside the port.


00:21:43.535 --> 00:21:45.165
That's impossible.


00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:46.450
Something is behind the port.


00:21:46.485 --> 00:21:47.665
We have to wake the crew now.


00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:51.500
No, the hibernation
phases must be kept intact.


00:21:51.535 --> 00:21:54.865
But why don't you show it to me?


00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:57.200
The rules say, that under
exceptional circumstances...


00:21:57.235 --> 00:21:58.861
...we have to wake
up the captain.


00:22:06.700 --> 00:22:10.179
It seems as if Dr. Portmann isn't
able to handle loneliness very well.


00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:15.358
I'm sorry that
we've awakened you.


00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:21.882
Let's just hope
that you are sure.


00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:17.713
The suits have been thrown around
because of the over pressure.


00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:52.395
The compartment was open for
several times throughout your shift.


00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:57.378
I hope for you that this
was just a technical failure.


00:25:40.700 --> 00:25:43.118
Let's go.


00:26:11.791 --> 00:26:14.208
The cargo compartment is
split up into 9 sectors.


00:26:14.243 --> 00:26:15.971
You take A to C.


00:26:16.006 --> 00:26:17.665
You take D to F.


00:26:17.700 --> 00:26:19.460
And I'll take the rest.


00:26:19.495 --> 00:26:22.028
Shouldn't we stay together?


00:26:22.063 --> 00:26:24.561
I don't want to stay overnight.


00:26:26.159 --> 00:26:27.533
We'll stay in contact...


00:26:49.900 --> 00:26:51.765
The containers are all locked.


00:26:51.800 --> 00:26:56.013
That is correct, you
should know that Decker.


00:27:42.200 --> 00:27:44.950
Didn't find anything
suspicious 'till now.


00:27:44.985 --> 00:27:47.700
Except that we are not
fully loaded. Answer.


00:27:47.735 --> 00:27:49.865
Me neither.


00:27:49.900 --> 00:27:52.200
Roger. Keep searching. Over.


00:28:05.700 --> 00:28:09.080
Lacroix, here Laura.


00:28:11.200 --> 00:28:12.752
Lacroix!


00:28:15.700 --> 00:28:17.000
Fuck!


00:28:17.700 --> 00:28:19.550
Decker?


00:28:19.585 --> 00:28:21.365
Decker!


00:28:21.400 --> 00:28:21.865
"What happened?"


00:28:21.900 --> 00:28:23.400
I think Lacroix has fallen down.


00:28:23.435 --> 00:28:24.700
"What? Where are you?"


00:28:24.735 --> 00:28:26.350
In sector E4-20.


00:28:26.385 --> 00:28:27.700
I'm going down to sector G.


00:28:27.735 --> 00:28:29.349
"I'm coming!"


00:28:40.700 --> 00:28:41.465
Lacroix!


00:28:41.500 --> 00:28:43.230
Do you hear me?


00:28:44.900 --> 00:28:46.913
Lacroix, do you hear me?


00:28:49.200 --> 00:28:50.065
Is he alive?


00:28:50.100 --> 00:28:52.031
We must get him
out of the cold now!


00:28:58.200 --> 00:29:00.700
The gate!


00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:09.500
According to the regulations,
I'll be in command of the ship.


00:31:09.535 --> 00:31:12.665
Prokoff, Vespucci fix the gate.


00:31:12.700 --> 00:31:15.700
The cargo compartment must
be sealed as soon as possible.


00:31:15.735 --> 00:31:18.700
Yoshida, you'll verify all
entrys in the main computer...


00:31:18.735 --> 00:31:20.867
...and check for
suspicious activities.


00:31:20.902 --> 00:31:23.000
And you will examine
Lacroixs corpse.


00:31:23.035 --> 00:31:26.230
I want the exact cause of death.


00:32:20.400 --> 00:32:22.071
Start recording.


00:32:27.700 --> 00:32:30.256
Multiple spline fracture.


00:32:34.700 --> 00:32:37.700
Craniocerebral injury.


00:32:39.700 --> 00:32:42.936
Supposedly caused by a
fall from a severe height.


00:32:43.700 --> 00:32:46.446
Time of Death: Some
minutes after the impact.


00:34:24.700 --> 00:34:27.200
I thought that we were just
transporting construction materials.


00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:29.900
That's what I was thinking too.


00:35:01.000 --> 00:35:01.965
Whats wrong with the gate?


00:35:02.000 --> 00:35:07.700
The fuck is. Everything is stuck
and the gears seem to be broken too.


00:35:33.800 --> 00:35:35.700
It must have been here.


00:35:38.100 --> 00:35:39.449
Sealed.


00:35:42.800 --> 00:35:45.055
I have Lacroix's batch.


00:37:04.000 --> 00:37:06.265
A child.


00:37:06.300 --> 00:37:08.189
It's a child!


00:37:15.028 --> 00:37:17.585
All containers
are full of humans.


00:37:24.700 --> 00:37:26.911
"Vespucci, Prokoff. "


00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:31.665
Yes?


00:37:31.700 --> 00:37:34.852
"Please come to sector F7-21."


00:37:42.900 --> 00:37:46.700
Why the heck do we transport
humans to Station 42?


00:37:57.200 --> 00:37:59.025
Fuuuuuuuu


00:38:01.200 --> 00:38:02.843
Thats really...


00:38:09.200 --> 00:38:10.198
Shit!


00:38:13.500 --> 00:38:16.100
Get moving!


00:38:16.135 --> 00:38:18.700
Go go go!


00:38:21.200 --> 00:38:22.638
Laura!


00:38:28.700 --> 00:38:29.775
Laura!


00:40:29.900 --> 00:40:31.200
What's going on in here?


00:40:32.100 --> 00:40:34.100
The containers
are full of humans.


00:40:41.900 --> 00:40:44.300
The cargo is the shipping
companies business.


00:40:44.335 --> 00:40:45.965
Lacroix was murdered.


00:40:46.000 --> 00:40:47.865
Lacroix opened the door
and because of the...


00:40:47.900 --> 00:40:51.100
...containers over pressure he
had been pushed in to the abyss.


00:40:51.135 --> 00:40:54.567
Someone set the containers in
motion and we got almost killed.


00:40:54.602 --> 00:40:57.965
The containers are moving
automatically, to prevent freezing.


00:40:58.000 --> 00:41:01.148
That's the reason why it's forbidden
to be in the cargo compartment.


00:41:01.183 --> 00:41:03.041
Somebody is on
board of the ship.


00:41:03.076 --> 00:41:04.865
He killed Lacroix
and almost us too.


00:41:04.900 --> 00:41:06.872
Did you know that there were
humans in the containers?


00:41:10.100 --> 00:41:13.229
This tank will be
returned immediately.


00:41:13.264 --> 00:41:14.630
This is a human!


00:41:16.000 --> 00:41:18.871
As a doctor, I am responsible
for the people on board.


00:41:18.906 --> 00:41:20.557
And I will examine
this girl now.


00:41:20.592 --> 00:41:22.665
Exactly what I was thinking.


00:41:22.700 --> 00:41:26.165
And furthermore I am authorized to
inspect any incident on this ship.


00:41:26.200 --> 00:41:29.200
The containers with the tanks may have
something to do with Lacroix's death.


00:41:29.700 --> 00:41:31.296
Then do your duty.


00:41:31.331 --> 00:41:35.105
But you can be sure that I
will report this incident.


00:41:46.000 --> 00:41:49.138
Inspecting tank.
Starting record.


00:42:01.300 --> 00:42:04.300
No usable scans from
the abdomen retrievable.


00:42:04.335 --> 00:42:07.266
Switching to high frequency.


00:42:13.700 --> 00:42:16.365
HF scans in the
head area possible.


00:42:16.400 --> 00:42:19.789
The girl shows some
minor brain activity.


00:42:19.824 --> 00:42:23.179
I assume a coma
caused by hibernation.


00:42:26.200 --> 00:42:29.915
Stopping record.


00:42:30.500 --> 00:42:32.946
Did you find something?


00:42:33.900 --> 00:42:37.200
It will take some time
to have precise results.


00:42:37.235 --> 00:42:38.756
May I help?


00:42:38.791 --> 00:42:40.243
Yes, maybe.


00:42:40.278 --> 00:42:45.668
The tank is blocking the scanner and
it's secured with an electronic lock.


00:43:02.500 --> 00:43:05.198
Did you find something?


00:43:07.500 --> 00:43:11.665
I need anything you
can find on Decker.


00:43:11.700 --> 00:43:16.541
Something is wrong with him.
He should be on our side.


00:43:25.900 --> 00:43:26.565
And?


00:43:26.600 --> 00:43:29.500
Because of an asymetric
RSA encryption.


00:43:29.535 --> 00:43:32.223
Could take some time.


00:43:46.800 --> 00:43:49.918
What do you know
about Station 42?


00:43:49.953 --> 00:43:52.665
En uninhabited station.


00:43:52.700 --> 00:43:57.200
Is officially being upgraded to a
transport hub for ships heading to Proxima.


00:43:57.235 --> 00:43:59.700
And inofficially?


00:44:01.500 --> 00:44:03.800
Why did you enlist
for this mission?


00:44:03.835 --> 00:44:05.567
I need money, that's it.


00:44:05.602 --> 00:44:07.300
You want to go to Rhea.


00:44:07.335 --> 00:44:08.467
Yes.


00:44:08.502 --> 00:44:09.565
Why?


00:44:09.600 --> 00:44:12.465
My sister lives on Rhea.


00:44:12.500 --> 00:44:17.700
She won the visa to
Rhea seven years ago.


00:44:17.735 --> 00:44:20.568
She is living our dream.


00:44:57.700 --> 00:45:01.067
Probably the automatic
sorting again.


00:45:08.100 --> 00:45:11.405
And if there is really
something on board?


00:45:11.440 --> 00:45:14.710
Fuck it. Let's just try
to fix this mess asap.


00:45:56.000 --> 00:45:58.442
Starting record.


00:46:04.400 --> 00:46:09.404
The girls brain is marbled
with an anorganic tissue.


00:46:09.439 --> 00:46:12.396
Entry of the tissue
into the body.


00:46:12.431 --> 00:46:15.734
Cervical C4, neck spline.


00:46:17.100 --> 00:46:20.000
Looks like ingrowth.


00:46:20.035 --> 00:46:22.437
Or pitted.


00:46:31.100 --> 00:46:32.865
A VR connector.


00:46:32.900 --> 00:46:34.765
Appearantly a perfected one.


00:46:34.800 --> 00:46:36.365
I've never seen
something like this.


00:46:36.400 --> 00:46:38.800
We could connect her
to an external system.


00:46:38.835 --> 00:46:40.965
That's too dangerous.


00:46:41.000 --> 00:46:44.665
That could lead to
irreperable neural damages.


00:46:44.700 --> 00:46:46.700
That's the only way to get more
information about the access.


00:46:46.735 --> 00:46:48.165
Under no circumstances.


00:46:48.200 --> 00:46:51.200
I will not risk this kids life.


00:46:52.700 --> 00:46:54.455
Well.


00:46:56.100 --> 00:46:59.562
For now, keep this
examinations results between us.


00:46:59.597 --> 00:47:01.405
Ok?


00:47:16.200 --> 00:47:17.700
Hi Hanna.


00:47:18.500 --> 00:47:20.214
So much stuff is
going on in here...


00:47:20.249 --> 00:47:21.928
...that I would like
to share with you.


00:47:23.000 --> 00:47:26.007
Why are we that far
away from each other?


00:47:26.042 --> 00:47:29.015
And it takes ages for
the messages to arrive.


00:47:29.900 --> 00:47:32.800
I just don't understand what's
happening on board anymore.


00:47:32.835 --> 00:47:35.500
We found a girl in
the cargo compartement.


00:47:35.535 --> 00:47:38.500
I'm trying to help her.


00:47:40.000 --> 00:47:41.765
We'll see each other soon.


00:47:41.800 --> 00:47:44.966
And then I'll tell
you everything.


00:48:31.000 --> 00:48:34.265
I was so delighted to
receive your message!


00:48:34.300 --> 00:48:38.500
It's so good to hear your voice
and know that you are alive.


00:48:41.800 --> 00:48:44.500
You found a girl?


00:48:44.535 --> 00:48:47.165
I don't get it.


00:48:47.200 --> 00:48:49.765
I would like to talk
to you in person.


00:48:49.800 --> 00:48:53.700
Why is it taking so long
for our messages to arrive.


00:48:53.735 --> 00:48:55.765
Laura listen.


00:48:55.800 --> 00:48:59.000
We don't want you to do
any more cargo flights.


00:48:59.035 --> 00:49:00.465
Come directly to Rhea.


00:49:00.500 --> 00:49:03.750
You could stay
with us for a while.


00:49:03.785 --> 00:49:07.000
We will prepare a
room for you and...


00:49:07.035 --> 00:49:09.200
I'm anticipating your arrival.


00:49:09.235 --> 00:49:12.003
Soon you'll be with us.


00:49:33.700 --> 00:49:36.722
I don't get what's
happening here.


00:49:41.000 --> 00:49:44.202
How is it possible that my
sister answers this fast?


00:49:48.400 --> 00:49:51.781
Why do you have knowledge
about neuronal accesses?


00:49:56.000 --> 00:49:59.558
Why shouldn't I tell anybody
about the examination?


00:50:02.600 --> 00:50:05.958
What do you know about
the people in the tanks?


00:50:10.400 --> 00:50:13.095
Who the hell are you?


00:51:56.391 --> 00:52:01.700
Everybody report
to the bridge asap.


00:52:03.700 --> 00:52:09.065
Yoshida scanned all log entries
and compared them with the backup.


00:52:09.100 --> 00:52:16.979
She discovered that a crew member manipulated
the log files of the cryo chambers.


00:52:18.800 --> 00:52:23.600
Why didn't you tell us that you have
been awakened on a regular basis?


00:52:23.635 --> 00:52:27.165
It's part of my duties to
check the ship periodically.


00:52:27.200 --> 00:52:31.300
So you are not denying that you left
the cryo chambers without our knowledge.


00:52:31.335 --> 00:52:33.665
No, that is correct.


00:52:33.700 --> 00:52:35.400
Where have you been
when Lacroix died?


00:52:35.435 --> 00:52:38.386
I knew it! Damn Snitch!


00:52:39.700 --> 00:52:42.645
I was in sector F5-17.


00:52:42.680 --> 00:52:48.715
And you can't demand an account
for the work I am doing for RBS.


00:52:48.750 --> 00:52:50.297
Arrest him.


00:52:51.600 --> 00:52:53.274
Put your weapon away!


00:52:55.900 --> 00:52:58.450
I have immunity. You know that.


00:52:58.485 --> 00:53:01.000
Not if you are
suspected of murder.


00:53:01.035 --> 00:53:03.654
Put your weapon away!


00:53:27.200 --> 00:53:30.700
I might have believed
you if you hadn't resited.


00:53:31.900 --> 00:53:34.500
Vespucci how much more time
do you need with the gate?


00:53:34.535 --> 00:53:36.477
48 hours.


00:53:39.700 --> 00:53:43.165
Dr. Portmann return that tank
to the cargo compartment asap.


00:53:43.200 --> 00:53:48.600
That's impossible. I gave the patient
a drug that regresses the filaments.


00:53:48.635 --> 00:53:50.900
She is not stable.
She can't be returned.


00:53:50.935 --> 00:53:52.665
That's none of my business!


00:53:52.700 --> 00:53:55.100
I want that tank returned
before the gate is fixed.


00:53:55.135 --> 00:53:56.906
This is an order!


00:53:56.941 --> 00:53:58.678
Do you understand?


00:54:01.700 --> 00:54:03.965
Get him to the cryo chambers.


00:54:04.000 --> 00:54:05.665
He must go to the
medical station first.


00:54:05.700 --> 00:54:11.659
I must treat his wounds or the blood
will contaminate the cooling fluid.


00:54:39.200 --> 00:54:41.114
You are doing your job well.


00:54:46.700 --> 00:54:50.339
Did you receive another
message from your sister?


00:55:25.800 --> 00:55:29.033
Vespucci, medical
station please.


00:55:29.068 --> 00:55:29.965
Laura!


00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:31.872
Laura wait!


00:55:37.300 --> 00:55:40.200
We are not flying to Station 42.


00:55:41.200 --> 00:55:43.557
Where are we heading then?


00:55:44.700 --> 00:55:47.808
To Rhea.


00:56:36.900 --> 00:56:39.265
Could you do me a favour?


00:56:39.300 --> 00:56:44.465
Would you please take a look if we
are really heading for Station 42?


00:57:21.200 --> 00:57:23.665
And?


00:57:23.700 --> 00:57:26.165
I was on the bridge and
locked into the system.


00:57:26.200 --> 00:57:29.917
The target coordinates of our
flight are well protected, but...


00:57:29.952 --> 00:57:36.100
...I can tell you for certain that
we are not heading for Station 42.


00:57:36.135 --> 00:57:39.165
And it's definite too that...


00:57:39.200 --> 00:57:44.000
...nobody would've been able to change
the coordinates while the journey.


00:57:44.035 --> 00:57:47.910
Because you can only set
them before the departure.


00:57:47.945 --> 00:57:53.965
I'm trying to spot where
else we might fly to.


00:57:54.000 --> 00:57:59.500
But that means that Decker wasn't
even able to change the coordinates.


00:57:59.535 --> 00:58:03.671
How long does it take a
message to arrive at Rhea?


00:58:04.500 --> 00:58:06.200
Probably half an
eternity. As always.


00:58:07.500 --> 00:58:09.332
Several years?


00:58:10.700 --> 00:58:15.009
My sister answered
me within 20 minutes.


00:58:15.044 --> 00:58:19.284
If that's true, then
Lindbergh lied to us.


00:58:19.319 --> 00:58:23.600
Only she has the logins
for the target coordinates.


00:58:23.635 --> 00:58:26.629
Decker told me that
we are flying to Rhea.


00:58:28.035 --> 00:58:30.700
Hey hey hey, look who's here!


00:58:30.735 --> 00:58:32.726
The gate has been fixed.


00:58:32.761 --> 00:58:36.537
And that's why Prokoff and I are throwing
a little party in the squad rooms.


00:58:38.200 --> 00:58:40.100
I don't have any
time. Got work to do.


00:58:40.135 --> 00:58:42.400
And what's with
our little party?


00:58:42.435 --> 00:58:45.165
Thanks for your help!


00:58:45.200 --> 00:58:47.765
But you are coming, right?


00:58:47.800 --> 00:58:52.187
We heated the room
just for this event.


00:59:05.400 --> 00:59:07.700
You won't stay that
long too, right?


00:59:09.200 --> 00:59:12.700
The last doctor left
afterwards for Rhea.


00:59:15.600 --> 00:59:19.365
Our lot will never be
able to afford that.


00:59:51.300 --> 00:59:54.479
Doesn't even taste that shitty!


01:00:11.298 --> 01:00:13.817
Probably the radiator.


01:00:20.188 --> 01:00:21.485
What are you doing?


01:00:22.102 --> 01:00:23.792
The party isn't over yet.


01:00:24.774 --> 01:00:26.448
I'll bring Yoshida some tea too.


01:00:28.712 --> 01:00:30.354
Ok... but hurry.


01:00:30.389 --> 01:00:33.330
And make sure Lindbergh
doesn't notice anything.


01:00:33.365 --> 01:00:35.244
She'd ruin our party.


01:00:36.169 --> 01:00:38.032
Don't worry, I'll be right back.


01:02:02.131 --> 01:02:03.529
Decker...


01:02:03.564 --> 01:02:05.873
That son of a bitch is gone.


01:02:07.921 --> 01:02:10.479
If I get my hands on him...


01:02:11.926 --> 01:02:13.842
He was woken up manually.


01:02:14.768 --> 01:02:16.684
Someone must have let him out.


01:02:16.719 --> 01:02:19.835
So we have a stowaway
on board after all.


01:02:19.870 --> 01:02:21.024
Crap...


01:02:21.806 --> 01:02:24.283
We'll search the whole ship.


01:02:24.318 --> 01:02:26.023
You go with Portmann.


01:02:26.058 --> 01:02:27.729
I'll go with Prokoff.


01:02:28.504 --> 01:02:30.148
We'll start on the main section.


01:02:30.183 --> 01:02:31.758
I'll lock all cargo bay access.


01:02:31.793 --> 01:02:34.242
If we don't find anything,
we'll check out the rest.


01:03:39.425 --> 01:03:41.022
Sick bay is clear.


01:03:41.057 --> 01:03:42.620
What's your situation?


01:03:43.543 --> 01:03:44.425
Nothing so far.


01:03:44.460 --> 01:03:46.246
We're at the sluice.


01:03:58.332 --> 01:03:59.792
There's something below us.


01:04:06.196 --> 01:04:08.331
Let's check out the lower deck.


01:04:32.789 --> 01:04:34.845
Looks like we have him.


01:04:34.880 --> 01:04:36.901
He must be in this duct.


01:04:40.901 --> 01:04:42.204
Ok... you go in here.


01:04:42.239 --> 01:04:44.377
I'll come from the other side.


01:04:44.412 --> 01:04:45.624
We'll kick his ass.


01:04:57.445 --> 01:05:01.276
Once he notices that I'm front
of him, he'll have to turn around.


01:05:01.311 --> 01:05:03.609
When you see him, you shoot.


01:05:03.644 --> 01:05:04.955
Boom, over and done.


01:05:04.990 --> 01:05:09.007
That bastard... he killed
Yoshida and Lacroix.


01:05:09.042 --> 01:05:09.699
Don't forget that.


01:07:07.124 --> 01:07:10.430
...blow... up...


01:09:09.136 --> 01:09:12.336
Everythings grows
again like it used to.


01:09:13.446 --> 01:09:15.594
We've been lied to
from the very beginning.


01:09:16.799 --> 01:09:17.983
These plants here...


01:09:18.018 --> 01:09:18.941
they're edible.


01:09:19.706 --> 01:09:23.613
The greenhouses keep
out the acid rain.


01:09:24.582 --> 01:09:28.314
We purify our own water
in underground tanks.


01:09:28.349 --> 01:09:32.046
We're completely
independent from the system.


01:09:32.081 --> 01:09:34.906
And we continue
to grow stronger.


01:09:34.941 --> 01:09:37.732
More people join us every day.


01:09:53.307 --> 01:09:54.131
Freeze!


01:09:56.815 --> 01:09:57.367
Laura..


01:09:57.402 --> 01:09:59.700
Thank god, you're alive.


01:09:59.735 --> 01:10:00.718
Calm down.


01:10:00.753 --> 01:10:01.826
Where the hell were you?


01:10:01.861 --> 01:10:03.567
We have everything
under control.


01:10:03.602 --> 01:10:04.795
We got him.


01:10:05.558 --> 01:10:06.562
Did you shoot?


01:10:10.633 --> 01:10:11.922
Who is that?


01:10:13.368 --> 01:10:14.188
Bruckner...


01:10:21.100 --> 01:10:22.947
What was your plan?


01:10:40.710 --> 01:10:42.475
No point in playing the hero.


01:10:43.444 --> 01:10:44.467
Bruckner is dead.


01:10:44.502 --> 01:10:46.065
Who are you trying to protect?


01:10:47.846 --> 01:10:50.595
Rhea... is a simulation, a lie.


01:10:52.888 --> 01:10:54.182
The people in the tanks...


01:10:54.217 --> 01:10:55.038
Bullshit.


01:10:55.073 --> 01:11:00.117
Their brains are beeing used as
neural units to create the simulation.


01:11:00.152 --> 01:11:02.399
We talk to the people
on Rhea all the time.


01:11:02.434 --> 01:11:04.323
Kuiper is lying
to all of humanity.


01:11:04.982 --> 01:11:06.407
Everything is covered up.


01:11:06.442 --> 01:11:07.396
Get him out of here.


01:11:08.075 --> 01:11:11.437
If people knew that parts of
earth are habitable again...


01:11:11.472 --> 01:11:14.228
the whole system
would break down.


01:11:15.183 --> 01:11:16.674
You killed him, didn't you?


01:11:18.713 --> 01:11:20.468
He went nuts.


01:11:20.503 --> 01:11:21.306
He killed Lacroix.


01:11:21.820 --> 01:11:23.243
And Yoshida?


01:11:25.733 --> 01:11:27.399
Move it.


01:11:35.996 --> 01:11:38.017
How's your little patient?


01:11:38.052 --> 01:11:38.757
Good.


01:11:40.456 --> 01:11:43.786
I think we can move her
back into the cargo hold.


01:11:44.926 --> 01:11:46.044
Excellent.


01:11:46.700 --> 01:11:48.674
Prokoff and Vespucci
will give you a hand.


01:11:49.392 --> 01:11:51.302
Then we can finally close
the cargo hold and...


01:11:51.337 --> 01:11:53.144
you'll go into crysleep.


01:11:53.179 --> 01:11:54.951
I will handle your shift.


01:12:43.705 --> 01:12:45.737
So.. you know about Rhea...


01:13:15.752 --> 01:13:18.199
The simulation is
only temporary...


01:13:24.252 --> 01:13:27.030
The colonization of Rhea was
a failure from the get-go.


01:13:30.040 --> 01:13:34.203
Our changes to the planet's ecosystem
caused unforeseen consequences.


01:13:36.826 --> 01:13:38.854
We will find another planet.


01:13:39.700 --> 01:13:42.719
And we won't repeat the
mistakes we made on Rhea.


01:13:43.640 --> 01:13:45.039
But until then...


01:13:45.074 --> 01:13:47.671
people need something
to keep them alive.


01:13:48.749 --> 01:13:50.236
And that thing is hope.


01:13:55.143 --> 01:13:58.959
What happens to those who find
out they're living in a simulation?


01:14:06.289 --> 01:14:08.622
The simulation is perfect...


01:14:08.657 --> 01:14:10.235
I was in there myself.


01:14:10.270 --> 01:14:13.363
It's impossible for
anyone to notice anything.


01:14:14.867 --> 01:14:16.811
Why are you doing all this?


01:14:21.700 --> 01:14:23.715
You just don't get it.


01:14:26.325 --> 01:14:28.407
Soon we'll be on Rhea.


01:14:28.442 --> 01:14:31.212
But you and your.. saboteur..
won't make it there alive.


01:14:31.247 --> 01:14:35.482
Noone will care about the death of
the ones who murdered the captain.


01:14:39.288 --> 01:14:41.595
Did you know that we
were going to Rhea?


01:15:10.777 --> 01:15:13.360
But... Rhea is a simulation...


01:15:13.395 --> 01:15:14.504
Who cares?


01:15:14.539 --> 01:15:16.581
Better than staying
on this piece of junk.


01:15:20.296 --> 01:15:22.244
What about all my plants?


01:15:22.279 --> 01:15:25.642
You idiot, there will be more
plants than you ever dreamed of.


01:15:26.385 --> 01:15:27.695
On Rhea, there is everything.


01:15:27.730 --> 01:15:28.437
Everything.


01:15:41.301 --> 01:15:43.198
I couldn't tell you the truth.


01:15:56.834 --> 01:15:59.911
Laura.. there's many
reasons not to trust me...


01:16:06.492 --> 01:16:09.744
But we are the only ones
who can finish this mission.


01:16:12.636 --> 01:16:13.694
Will you help me?


01:16:16.245 --> 01:16:18.375
Will you help me get
my sister out of there?


01:16:20.242 --> 01:16:22.239
We need two people to do this.


01:16:22.274 --> 01:16:24.015
It's impossible to enter
the simulation on your own.


01:16:25.028 --> 01:16:27.517
We'll dock at Station
42 according to plan.


01:16:28.236 --> 01:16:31.511
We can delay the cargo unload
procedure by 30 minutes.


01:16:31.546 --> 01:16:33.761
The Kassandra will then
unload automatically.


01:16:33.796 --> 01:16:35.976
Laura and me will be
flying to the station.


01:16:36.547 --> 01:16:39.134
And log into the
system right here.


01:16:39.169 --> 01:16:40.563
How's that going to work?


01:16:41.814 --> 01:16:45.377
The hardware used for connecting
is here, in the connection modules.


01:16:51.582 --> 01:16:57.545
I will connect Laura to the
simulation here on the main module.


01:16:58.148 --> 01:17:00.419
Once she's in, she will
send a message to Earth.


01:17:00.454 --> 01:17:02.690
Meanwhile, I'll go look
for her sister's tank.


01:17:04.800 --> 01:17:07.373
When we're done, we'll blow up the
transponder of the main antenna.


01:17:09.575 --> 01:17:11.478
The station itself
stays fully operational.


01:17:11.513 --> 01:17:12.760
That means...


01:17:12.795 --> 01:17:15.859
Everyone will keep
living in the simulation.


01:17:15.894 --> 01:17:17.736
But they won't be able
to send any more messages.


01:17:17.771 --> 01:17:19.435
Laura's message..


01:17:19.470 --> 01:17:21.100
will be the last.


01:17:21.878 --> 01:17:24.037
I hope people back
home will believe us.


01:18:03.610 --> 01:18:05.490
Is the Earth really
habitable again?


01:18:06.617 --> 01:18:08.279
We had 3 expeditions.


01:18:10.536 --> 01:18:12.360
Nature is rampant.


01:18:13.497 --> 01:18:14.805
She's talking everything back.


01:18:17.945 --> 01:18:20.692
Whole cities are grown
over up to the second floor.


01:18:25.052 --> 01:18:27.354
I'll bring Ariane back to Earth.


01:18:30.188 --> 01:18:31.996
There's millions
of tanks, Laura..


01:18:33.540 --> 01:18:35.678
Even if we do find her...


01:18:35.713 --> 01:18:38.795
I don't know in what
condition she'll be in.


01:18:39.956 --> 01:18:41.830
She was in the simulation
for a long time.


01:18:46.046 --> 01:18:47.406
We have to try.


01:18:48.466 --> 01:18:50.800
I want to show her the Earth...


01:19:47.913 --> 01:19:49.906
Has this interface
been used before?


01:19:50.511 --> 01:19:51.714
No, it's a prototype.


01:19:51.749 --> 01:19:54.541
It works like a neural
connection for the simulation.


01:20:02.908 --> 01:20:04.083
Don't be scared.


01:20:10.602 --> 01:20:12.152
27 minutes.


01:20:16.930 --> 01:20:18.083
Don't you think we should...


01:20:18.118 --> 01:20:20.101
What?


01:20:20.136 --> 01:20:23.188
I'm doing this for you,
and me. For both of us!


01:20:23.223 --> 01:20:24.346
As if I'll let this pass us by.


01:20:24.381 --> 01:20:27.424
We'll throw some guys out of
their tanks and go in ourselves.


01:20:27.459 --> 01:20:29.663
Once the ship is
unloaded, we'll be on Rhea!


01:20:41.795 --> 01:20:43.330
God damnit...


01:22:23.581 --> 01:22:23.989
Prokoff.


01:22:24.024 --> 01:22:24.720
Do you hear me?


01:22:24.755 --> 01:22:27.573
I have Lindbergh's card.


01:22:28.249 --> 01:22:32.362
Reprogram the unload timer
to 10 minutes, got it?


01:22:32.397 --> 01:22:34.385
Otherwise those 2
will make it back...


01:22:34.420 --> 01:22:36.374
and the containers
won't be unloaded...


01:22:36.409 --> 01:22:38.291
and we won't be on Rhea, got it?


01:22:46.254 --> 01:22:48.854
We have to hurry.. let's
meet in the cargo hold, ok?


01:22:54.118 --> 01:22:56.248
Decker? Can you hear me?


01:22:57.595 --> 01:23:00.271
I have problems
with my fuel cell.


01:23:06.756 --> 01:23:08.963
The cell is... *garbage*


01:23:11.680 --> 01:23:15.210
...under no
circumstances.. open.. gate


01:24:11.875 --> 01:24:13.362
Rhea here we come!


01:24:37.962 --> 01:24:40.059
...find.. cell...


01:24:41.012 --> 01:24:42.828
.. found nothing...


01:24:42.863 --> 01:24:44.644
...coming anyway...


01:24:47.143 --> 01:24:49.270
I don't think
that's a good ide...


01:24:49.305 --> 01:24:49.467
.. where you are...


01:24:49.502 --> 01:24:52.724
I'm trying to
find Ariane's tank.


01:24:52.759 --> 01:24:54.946
Laura... copy..?


01:25:30.902 --> 01:25:32.049
Decker, can you hear me?


01:25:32.084 --> 01:25:32.870
Decker!


01:25:33.529 --> 01:25:35.324
I can't control my
thrusters anymore!


01:25:37.333 --> 01:25:38.563
I'm drifting off!


01:25:41.849 --> 01:25:43.207
Decker! Where are you?!


01:26:21.832 --> 01:26:23.017
Decker.. where are you?


01:26:39.236 --> 01:26:40.287
I see you.


01:27:43.015 --> 01:27:44.669
I found Ariane's tank...


01:27:46.307 --> 01:27:47.240
Impossible...


01:27:49.119 --> 01:27:50.185
I'm sorry.


01:27:52.462 --> 01:27:53.347
I want to see her.


01:27:54.922 --> 01:27:57.419
Set the module to my
sister's simulation.


01:27:59.048 --> 01:28:00.856
I'll send the
message from there.


01:28:37.630 --> 01:28:40.311
The Kassandra.


01:28:48.812 --> 01:28:50.759
Prokoff and Vespucci...


01:28:50.794 --> 01:28:51.844
Those idiots.


01:28:52.368 --> 01:28:54.654
That means we have 7
minutes at the most...


01:28:54.689 --> 01:28:56.295
then I'll get you out manually.


01:28:56.330 --> 01:28:57.468
OK.


01:32:53.667 --> 01:32:55.539
Look how beatiful
we have it here...


01:32:59.748 --> 01:33:01.700
Finally you can actually see it.


01:33:01.735 --> 01:33:02.779
Finally...


01:33:04.628 --> 01:33:06.443
And your room is
almost ready too!


01:33:08.120 --> 01:33:09.391
You look beatiful.


01:33:11.361 --> 01:33:11.947
Come in.


01:33:12.823 --> 01:33:13.761
I'll show you everything.


01:33:15.069 --> 01:33:16.838
Kids, look who's here!


01:33:21.462 --> 01:33:22.704
Laura are you crying?


01:33:32.489 --> 01:33:35.255
Ariane, I have to
go for a minute.


01:33:36.590 --> 01:33:37.661
What's wrong?


01:33:39.108 --> 01:33:40.845
I love you, Ariane.


01:33:47.960 --> 01:33:49.476
Laura, where are you going?


01:34:47.032 --> 01:34:49.130
My name is Laura Portmann.


01:34:49.659 --> 01:34:51.712
This is the last
message from Rhea.


01:34:52.621 --> 01:34:54.598
Rhea is not paradise.


01:34:55.605 --> 01:34:57.794
Rhea is a simulation.


01:34:58.795 --> 01:35:00.485
We will bring you proof.


01:35:02.125 --> 01:35:03.811
We were all betrayed.


01:35:06.288 --> 01:35:08.836
Everything about Rhea is a lie.


01:35:10.087 --> 01:35:11.534
We don't need Rhea.


01:35:12.883 --> 01:35:14.946
However, we still have Earth.


01:35:15.670 --> 01:35:17.915
Earth is habitable again.


01:35:19.785 --> 01:35:23.409
Nobody will ever have
contact with Rhea again.


01:35:25.064 --> 01:35:26.311
We're destroying
the antennas now.


01:35:55.871 --> 01:35:56.735
Do you hear me?


01:35:57.863 --> 01:35:58.334
Yes.


01:36:00.179 --> 01:36:02.000
Good, we must hurry.


01:36:02.035 --> 01:36:03.688
The Kassandra could
launch anytime now...


01:36:05.556 --> 01:36:07.025
and you have to go
back on your own.


01:36:07.060 --> 01:36:08.365
On my own?


01:36:11.036 --> 01:36:11.698
Yes.


01:36:14.409 --> 01:36:16.073
I'm not leaving without you.


01:36:16.108 --> 01:36:17.263
You have to.


01:36:17.298 --> 01:36:20.154
We won't make it far
with just one jetpack.


01:36:20.189 --> 01:36:22.164
I gave you my fuel cell.


01:36:22.199 --> 01:36:25.687
It has enough fuel to
get you to the Kassandra.


01:36:25.722 --> 01:36:27.177
I'm not leaving without you.


01:36:30.026 --> 01:36:32.046
Go back to the girl.


01:36:32.081 --> 01:36:34.067
She's our only proof.


01:37:03.815 --> 01:37:04.509
Go.


01:37:08.120 --> 01:37:08.861
I can't!


01:37:08.896 --> 01:37:09.603
You can.


01:37:12.291 --> 01:37:12.917
No...


01:37:16.665 --> 01:37:17.835
I love you.


01:40:02.444 --> 01:40:03.380
Where is the girl!?


01:40:27.132 --> 01:40:29.595
Noone will be able to send
messages from Rhea now.


01:43:27.709 --> 01:43:30.103
My name is Laura Portmann.


01:43:30.138 --> 01:43:33.037
This is the last
message from Rhea.


01:43:34.318 --> 01:43:36.201
Rhea is not paradise.


01:43:36.969 --> 01:43:39.486
Rhea is a simulation.


01:43:40.248 --> 01:43:42.373
We will bring you proof.


01:43:43.376 --> 01:43:45.292
We were all betrayed.


01:43:47.048 --> 01:43:48.414
We don't need Rhea.


01:43:49.979 --> 01:43:52.559
However, we still
have have Earth.


01:43:52.594 --> 01:43:54.918
Earth is habitable again.


01:43:56.781 --> 01:44:01.604
Nobody will ever have
contact with Rhea again.


01:44:02.725 --> 01:44:04.409
We're destroying
the antennas now.


01:44:13.200 --> 01:44:15.800
Subtitled by


01:44:15.835 --> 01:44:18.417
PumpAction


01:44:18.452 --> 01:44:20.965
Surray


01:44:21.000 --> 01:44:23.700
and very special thanks to


01:44:23.735 --> 01:44:26.665
Zotten


01:44:26.700 --> 01:44:31.315
and our fellow humpers!

